81 a. Discovers in a report by the US Congress published on 3 February 20266a that in more than 90 meetings organised under the Anti-Disinformation Code between 2022 and 2024, the Commission reportedly pressured platforms to change their global content moderation rules and censor more content; Under pressure from the European Commission, TikTok removed or restricted statements such as “We need to stop the sexualisation of children”, even though they were part of common political debate, in the lead-up to Slovakia’s 2023 national parliamentary elections; Learns that the Commission has reportedly interfered and put pressure on several digital platforms during elections in several Member States; Calls on the Commission to immediately clarify the resources involved in the 2024 budget and to present itself spontaneously to parliamentarians to respond to the serious accusations listed in the report;

